== status
specctx status: Show the active changes, the current task, and the open questions.

Usage:
  `specctx status [flags]`

Flags:
  `--root <path>`              Use this project root.
  `--json`                     Print one JSON document.
  `--help`                     Show this help.

Exit codes:
  `0` Success.
  `2` A usage error.
  `3` An internal error.

Example:
  `specctx status`

== next
specctx next: Name the next action of the loop from the files on disk. Write nothing.

Usage:
  `specctx next [flags]`

Flags:
  `--change <name>`            Decide for this change. The key or the full folder name works.
  `--root <path>`              Use this project root.
  `--json`                     Print one JSON document.
  `--help`                     Show this help.

Exit codes:
  `0` Success.
  `2` A usage error.
  `3` An internal error.

Example:
  `specctx next --json`

== query
specctx query: Find the entries that contain all terms. With --change and no term, list every entry of that change.

Usage:
  `specctx query [term...] [flags]`

Flags:
  `--kind <kind>`              Show only entries of this kind. Any case works.
  `--change <name>`            Show only entries of this change. The key or the full folder name works.
  `--limit <n>`                Show n lines at most. The default is 20. Use 0 for no limit.
  `--all`                      Show all copies of an ID.
  `--root <path>`              Use this project root.
  `--json`                     Print one JSON document.
  `--help`                     Show this help.

Exit codes:
  `0` Success.
  `2` A usage error.
  `3` An internal error.

Example:
  `specctx query lockfile --kind req`

== related
specctx related: Show the entries that link to an ID, a file, or a change.

Usage:
  `specctx related <ID|path|change> [flags]`

Flags:
  `--depth <n>`                Follow links n steps. The default is 1.
  `--all`                      Show all copies of an ID.
  `--root <path>`              Use this project root.
  `--json`                     Print one JSON document.
  `--help`                     Show this help.

Exit codes:
  `0` Success.
  `2` A usage error, an unknown ID, or a path that is not a file in the repository.
  `3` An internal error.

Example:
  `specctx related src/graph/bundle.ts`

== bundle
specctx bundle: Print the spec text for the IDs, files, or changes and their links.

Usage:
  `specctx bundle <ID|path|change...> [flags]`

Flags:
  `--budget <n>`               Stop at n characters. The default is 8000.
  `--depth <n>`                Follow links n steps. The default is 1.
  `--all`                      Show all copies of an ID.
  `--block`                    Print only the requirement block, as it sits in the spec file. Each ID must be a requirement.
  `--root <path>`              Use this project root.
  `--json`                     Print one JSON document.
  `--help`                     Show this help.

Exit codes:
  `0` Success.
  `2` A usage error, an unknown ID, a bad path, or an ID that is not a requirement.
  `3` An internal error.

Example:
  `specctx bundle REQ-IDX-001 --budget 3000`

== check
specctx check: Find ID and link errors.

Usage:
  `specctx check [flags]`

Flags:
  `--strict`                   Also find gaps in tests and evidence.
  `--root <path>`              Use this project root.
  `--json`                     Print one JSON document.
  `--help`                     Show this help.

Exit codes:
  `0` No finding.
  `1` One finding or more.
  `2` A usage error.
  `3` An internal error.

Example:
  `specctx check --strict`

== gate
specctx gate: Run `check`, the baseline against the merge base of [gate] base, the markdown linters, `openspec validate` with the command in [gate] openspec, and the length check. Stop at the first failure.

Usage:
  `specctx gate [flags]`

Flags:
  `--strict`                   Run `check` and `openspec validate` in strict mode.
  `--markdown <globs>`         Lint these markdown globs instead of [gate] markdown. Separate them with spaces.
  `--rerun`                    Run only the rerun step. Run the command of each task that the range closed. Compare its exit code with the evidence.
  `--base <ref>`               With --rerun, take the merge base with this ref. The default is [gate] base.
  `--root <path>`              Use this project root.
  `--json`                     Print one JSON document.
  `--help`                     Show this help.

Exit codes:
  `0` Every step passed.
  `1` A step failed.
  `2` A usage error.
  `3` An internal error.

Example:
  `specctx gate --strict`

== task next
specctx task next: Show the next open task.

Usage:
  `specctx task next [flags]`

Flags:
  `--change <name>`            Look only in this change. The key or the full folder name works.
  `--root <path>`              Use this project root.
  `--json`                     Print one JSON document.
  `--help`                     Show this help.

Exit codes:
  `0` An open task.
  `1` No open task.
  `2` A usage error.
  `3` An internal error.

Example:
  `specctx task next --change 008`

== task verify
specctx task verify: Run the `Verify:` command of a task. Write nothing.

Usage:
  `specctx task verify <task> [flags]`

Flags:
  `--root <path>`              Use this project root.
  `--json`                     Print one JSON document.
  `--help`                     Show this help.

Exit codes:
  `0` The command passed.
  `1` The command failed.
  `2` A usage error.
  `3` An internal error.

Example:
  `specctx task verify 008/1.1`

== stats
specctx stats: Show five metrics for each change and the gate runs.

Usage:
  `specctx stats [flags]`

Flags:
  `--change <name>`            Show only this change.
  `--write`                    Also write docs/metrics/<date>.md.
  `--root <path>`              Use this project root.
  `--json`                     Print one JSON document.
  `--help`                     Show this help.

Exit codes:
  `0` Success.
  `2` A usage error.
  `3` An internal error.

Example:
  `specctx stats --write`

== lint tells
specctx lint tells: Find the AI writing tells in markdown files. Read stdin when no file is given.

Usage:
  `specctx lint tells <file...> [flags]`

Flags:
  `--baseline <n>`             Exit 0 when the hard findings are n or fewer. The default is 0.
  `--disable <rules>`          Ignore these rules. Separate them with commas.
  `--json`                     Print the findings as JSON.
  `--selftest`                 Run the built in tests of the linter.
  `--help`                     Show this help.

Exit codes:
  `0` The hard findings are at the baseline or below.
  `1` The hard findings are over the baseline.
  `2` A usage error.

Example:
  `specctx lint tells --baseline 0 README.md`

== lint ste
specctx lint ste: Find the breaks of the structural STE rules in markdown files. Read stdin when no file is given.

Usage:
  `specctx lint ste <file...> [flags]`

Flags:
  `--baseline <n>`             Exit 0 when the hard findings are n or fewer. The default is 0.
  `--disable <rules>`          Ignore these rules. Separate them with commas.
  `--json`                     Print the findings as JSON.
  `--selftest`                 Run the built in tests of the linter.
  `--help`                     Show this help.

Exit codes:
  `0` The hard findings are at the baseline or below.
  `1` The hard findings are over the baseline.
  `2` A usage error.

Example:
  `specctx lint ste --baseline 0 README.md`

== build
specctx build: Write the index to .ctx/index.json.

Usage:
  `specctx build [flags]`

Flags:
  `--root <path>`              Use this project root.
  `--json`                     Print one JSON document.
  `--help`                     Show this help.

Exit codes:
  `0` Success.
  `2` A usage error.
  `3` An internal error.

Example:
  `specctx build`

== id new
specctx id new: Print the next free ID. The kind is REQ, SCN, ADR, or DEC.

Usage:
  `specctx id new <kind> <code> [flags]`

Flags:
  `--for <REQ-ID>`             Give the requirement of a new scenario.
  `--count <n>`                Print n IDs in sequence.
  `--root <path>`              Use this project root.
  `--json`                     Print one JSON document.
  `--help`                     Show this help.

Exit codes:
  `0` Success.
  `2` A usage error or an unknown code.
  `3` An internal error.

Example:
  `specctx id new REQ IDX`

== id retire
specctx id retire: Add an ID to decisions/retired-ids.md.

Usage:
  `specctx id retire <ID> <reason> [flags]`

Flags:
  `--root <path>`              Use this project root.
  `--json`                     Print one JSON document.
  `--help`                     Show this help.

Exit codes:
  `0` Success.
  `2` A usage error, or the ID is still in use.
  `3` An internal error.

Example:
  `specctx id retire REQ-IDX-009 merged into REQ-IDX-001`

== task start
specctx task start: Print the bundle of a task and set it as the current task.

Usage:
  `specctx task start <task> [flags]`

Flags:
  `--root <path>`              Use this project root.
  `--json`                     Print one JSON document.
  `--help`                     Show this help.

Exit codes:
  `0` Success.
  `2` A usage error, or the task is done or unknown.
  `3` An internal error.

Example:
  `specctx task start 008/1.1`

== task done
specctx task done: Run the `Verify:` command. On success, write the evidence and set the checkbox.

Usage:
  `specctx task done <task> [flags]`

Flags:
  `--manual <note>`            Record a manual note. A task with no `Verify:` command needs this flag.
  `--root <path>`              Use this project root.
  `--json`                     Print one JSON document.
  `--help`                     Show this help.

Exit codes:
  `0` Success.
  `1` The `Verify:` command failed. The task stays open.
  `2` A usage error.
  `3` An internal error.

Example:
  `specctx task done 008/1.1`

== task reopen
specctx task reopen: Clear the checkbox and keep the old evidence.

Usage:
  `specctx task reopen <task> <why> [flags]`

Flags:
  `--root <path>`              Use this project root.
  `--json`                     Print one JSON document.
  `--help`                     Show this help.

Exit codes:
  `0` Success.
  `2` A usage error.
  `3` An internal error.

Example:
  `specctx task reopen 008/1.1 the spec changed`

== handoff write
specctx handoff write: Write .ctx/handoff.md from the index and the evidence.

Usage:
  `specctx handoff write [flags]`

Flags:
  `--root <path>`              Use this project root.
  `--json`                     Print one JSON document.
  `--help`                     Show this help.

Exit codes:
  `0` Success.
  `2` A usage error.
  `3` An internal error.

Example:
  `specctx handoff write`

== handoff ask
specctx handoff ask: Add an open question to the handoff.

Usage:
  `specctx handoff ask <question> [flags]`

Flags:
  `--change <name>`            Give the question to this change, not to the current task. The key or the full folder name works.
  `--plan`                     Mark the question as the plan approval. Only this mark ends the plan stop. It needs --change.
  `--root <path>`              Use this project root.
  `--json`                     Print one JSON document.
  `--help`                     Show this help.

Exit codes:
  `0` Success.
  `2` A usage error.
  `3` An internal error.

Example:
  `specctx handoff ask --change 008 --plan "plan ready for 008-tasks. Approve to start the tasks?"`

== handoff resolve
specctx handoff resolve: Move open question n to the resolved list.

Usage:
  `specctx handoff resolve <n> <answer> [flags]`

Flags:
  `--root <path>`              Use this project root.
  `--json`                     Print one JSON document.
  `--help`                     Show this help.

Exit codes:
  `0` Success.
  `2` A usage error.
  `3` An internal error.

Example:
  `specctx handoff resolve 1 "yes, for one release"`

== init
specctx init: Write a default spec-ctx.toml file.

Usage:
  `specctx init [flags]`

Flags:
  `--schema`                   Also install the ID templates and add the spec-ctx rules to openspec/config.yaml.
  `--skills`                   Also install the specctx-run skill and its aliases in .claude/skills and .agents/skills.
  `--all`                      Do all three.
  `--force`                    Replace the files that have other content. spec-ctx.toml stays.
  `--root <path>`              Use this project root.
  `--json`                     Print one JSON document.
  `--help`                     Show this help.

Exit codes:
  `0` Success.
  `2` A usage error.
  `3` An internal error.

Example:
  `specctx init --all`

== adopt
specctx adopt: Write IDs into the headers of the main specs and the active deltas. Undo on a new finding.

Usage:
  `specctx adopt [flags]`

Flags:
  `--dry-run`                  Show the ID that each header without an ID gets. Write nothing.
  `--root <path>`              Use this project root.
  `--json`                     Print one JSON document.
  `--help`                     Show this help.

Exit codes:
  `0` The IDs are written, or nothing is left to adopt.
  `1` The dry run found headers to adopt, or a new finding undid the write.
  `2` A usage error.
  `3` An internal error.

Example:
  `specctx adopt --dry-run`

